    (property "Note" "Power-fail ride-through. With the sensor rail shed and the LEDs off the board draws about 0.35 W here, so the bank holds the rails up long enough to finish the block in flight and close the file. 16x22 rather than 16x17.5: the two footprints are identical in every copper and courtyard layer -- only the can is 4.5 mm taller -- so the extra 220 uF costs nothing but enclosure height. Any 330uF >=80V on a 16 mm land works; match in the JLC catalogue at order. Pin 1 is +" (at 121.92 57.66 0)
